A||N||2||strick8||Speed Sensor Gear||||9||
Z||000000||strick8||05-03-2000||07:51 PM||||My Speed Sensor gear broke about a week ago and I put one on order.  But since that time my service engine light came on.  Three codes came up 24,25,35.  Well I expected the 24 (Vehicle Speed Sensor fault) but not the others.  So I reset the ECM drove for a day and then codes 24,35(Idle Air Control fault) came up.  So I went and bought a new IAC and installed it.  Reset the ECM and took for a drive.  The car has never run worse. It will hold an idle at rest but if I’m doing 40 and push in the clutch it will stall.  My question is this because the IAC needs the VSS to reset or is something else wrong.  My Haynes manual tells me the VSS controls the operation of the TCC (Transaxle Converter Clutch) and the IAC.  I have checked all vacuum lines and sensor connection.  I hope when my VSS gear is installed this problem will be fixed.  Should I get my hopes ||||reg||9
Z||000001||TOM||05-03-2000||10:38 PM||||If its not broke dont fix it. Driving it with the vss not conected or broken like the case may be will give you all kinds of stuff. It thinks the car is not moving but all this stuff is going on. Put the old iac in and wait till the gear comes in to try the reset and go thing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||strick8||05-04-2000||10:33 PM||||Well I put in the Speed Sensor gear and it now runs terrific.  I not sure what it has to do with my AC but that was not working properly either without the gear.  Never knew the Speed Sensor did anything but tell you how fast you are going.  All I know is my car run’s terrible without it.||||reg||10
